                <pb facs="0398" n="372" xml:id="pg372"/>

                <head>186. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>At 7 p.m. Foreign Secretary Macmillan met with Secretary of State Dulles at the
                    latter’s villa to review the events of the day and discuss the Middle East. The
                    only record of this meeting is a one-sentence notation, which indicates that
                    Merchant, MacArthur, Bowie, and Phleger were also present, in Merchant, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Recollections</hi>, page 32.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
